# MFA Platform — RAG rules

Reference: **`docs/RAG.md`**

## Retrieve-first

No LLM generation without an evidence pack. If retrieval score &lt; threshold → respond `insufficient` + `human_review`.

## Response contract (required fields)

`answer`, `confidence`, `citations[]`, `top_signals[]`, `recommended_action`, `limitations`

## Query routing

- Structured lookups ("why is X MFA?") → SQL first, vector optional
- Semantic ("similar sites") → OpenSearch k-NN (RAG v2 only)
- Change detection → diff `signal_snapshot` versions

## Citation validator

Every factual claim in `answer` must reference a `citations[].id` from the retrieved pack. Reject and regenerate on mismatch.

## Chunk metadata

Filter by `domain`, `url_id`, `signal_version`, `doc_type` on every vector query.

## Cost controls

- Cache grounded responses 24h keyed by `evidence_hash`
- Token caps per query; batch off-peak for bulk indexing

## Do not

- Invent policy rules not in retrieved policy chunks
- Return answers without `recommended_action`
- Skip `limitations` when evidence is partial
